# The build context is the patched swipl-devel tree, and this file decides
# which of its packages the host is built with: tools/wasm-host/Dockerfile
# hands cmake every packages/*/CMakeLists.txt the context holds as
# SWIPL_PACKAGE_LIST, so an entry here is the whole of adding a package.
#
# The base set is upstream's: npm-swipl-wasm clones swipl-devel without
# --recursive and initialises exactly twelve package submodules
# (docker/Dockerfile at the commit tools/wasm-host/wasm.pin names:
#   packages/chr packages/clib packages/clpqr packages/http packages/json
#   packages/nlp packages/pcre packages/plunit packages/sgml packages/RDF
#   packages/semweb packages/zlib).
# tools/pymetta-host/fetch-source.sh checks out every submodule, because the
# native host builds far more, so the rest are excluded here.
#
# Four are ours. packages/archive, packages/utf8proc and packages/yaml are
# SWI's own bindings for library(archive), library(unicode) and library(yaml),
# which lib_compression, lib_unicode and lib_yaml import; no swipl-wasm
# release has carried them, and the Dockerfile builds the C libraries they
# link (utf8proc through pkg-config, which the image now installs; its absence
# is what stopped the first build of this image, measured 2026-09-23).
# packages/metta is staged by tools/wasm-host/build.sh and holds the library
# pack's own native halves.
#
# The excluded entries are submodules the host leaves out; the plain files
# under packages/ (README, cmake/, index.html) are kept, as a clone has them.
bench
debian
packages/*
!packages/README
!packages/cmake
!packages/index.html
!packages/chr
!packages/clib
!packages/clpqr
!packages/http
!packages/json
!packages/nlp
!packages/pcre
!packages/plunit
!packages/sgml
!packages/RDF
!packages/semweb
!packages/zlib
!packages/archive
!packages/utf8proc
!packages/yaml
!packages/metta
